                <pb facs="0549" n="461" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg461"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Clayton.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraph rase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-01-28"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay instructs Mr. Clayton to inquire into the circumstances connected with
                    the imprisonment of Harding and Dugat, which took place at Matamoros, for a
                    technical but insignificant infraction of local laws, and if the facts in the
                    case seem to warrant it to use his good offices to effect their release.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
